---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FersAnnuityCalculator from '../../components/FersAnnuityCalculator';
---

<Layout
  title="FERS Basic Annuity Calculator | FersMath"
  description="Calculate your full FERS basic annuity from your High-3 average salary, years of service, and a survivor benefit election, including the 1.1% age-62 multiplier, MRA+10 early retirement and postponing it, VERA and discontinued service retirement, and the law enforcement/firefighter/ATC special provision."
>
  <main style="min-height: 100vh; background: #f8fafc; padding: 2rem 1rem;">
    <div style="max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto;">

      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #64748b;">
        <a href="/" style="color: #2A7D9C; text-decoration: none;">Home</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem;">›</span>
        <span>FERS Basic Annuity Calculator</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- OPM Rules notice -->
      <div style="background: #eff6ff; border: 1px solid #bfdbfe; border-radius: 0.75rem;
                  padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #1e40af;">
        <strong>OPM Rule:</strong> Annuity = High-3 average salary × years of service × 1%
        (1.1% if you're retiring at age 62 or older with 20+ years of service). Law enforcement
        officers, firefighters, and air traffic controllers use 1.7% on their first 20 years of
        covered service and 1% beyond that instead. Retiring at your Minimum Retirement Age with 10
        to 29 years (MRA+10) reduces the annuity 5/12 of 1% for each full month you're under 62 when
        it starts, unless you have 20+ years and it starts at 60 or later. With a VERA offer or an
        involuntary (discontinued service) separation, you can retire at 50 with 20 years or at any
        age with 25, with no age reduction. A full survivor election
        reduces your annuity 10% and pays your spouse 50% of it; a partial election reduces it 5% for
        a 25% survivor benefit. Source: OPM's FERS computation, eligibility, types-of-retirement and
        survivor benefit pages, 5 U.S.C. 8414(b) and 8421, 5 CFR 842.403–842.404 and 843.306, and
        the CSRS/FERS Handbook, Chapter 46.
      </div>

      <!-- React calculator — client:load so it hydrates immediately -->
      <FersAnnuityCalculator client:load />

      <!-- Disclaimer -->
      <div style="margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; background: #fff;
                  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 0.75rem;
                  font-size: 0.8rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.6;">
        <strong style="color: #64748b;">Disclaimer:</strong> This tool is for educational
        purposes only and covers immediate retirement only (62 with 5 years, 60 with 20, your
        Minimum Retirement Age with 30 or with 10, VERA or discontinued service retirement, or the law
        enforcement/firefighter/ATC special provision). It does not model deferred retirement,
        disability retirement, separation incentive (VSIP) payments, CSRS, unused sick
        leave credit, or annual cost-of-living adjustments. Always verify your annuity estimate with
        your agency HR office or OPM before making retirement decisions.
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
